  bootwright / machine exec
      Run a command over SSH. By default, log in with the Machine's SSH identity. Select a
      different account with --ssh-user and its --ssh-id-file or --ssh-ask-password. Password
      prompts require a terminal and one target. An unproved host key requires interactive
      confirmation before SSH offers a credential. The exit status is the client's. --name
      takes a comma-separated list: the command runs on every listed machine concurrently, at
      most eight at a time, each output line is prefixed by its machine, and the exit status is
      the highest any client returned. Bootwright flags go before the command. Use -- before a
      flag-shaped first payload value to preserve it as data. After the first payload value,
      all remaining tokens belong to the payload.

  Usage
    bootwright machine exec <command>... [flags]

  Command flags
      --name  Select comma-separated machine names (required)

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright machine exec --context lab --name node -- uname -a
